From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kelvin Jiang <kelvinjiang@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:15:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] [DNR] Require host permissions for response header
 value matching rules

Matching on response header values (via `values` or `excludedValues` in
`responseHeaders` or `excludedResponseHeaders`) can allow extensions to
infer sensitive information from responses for requests they do not have
host permissions for.

To prevent this:
- Restrict response header value matching without host permissions to an
  allowlist of safe headers (CORS-safelisted response headers and
  `Content-Encoding`). Matching only on header presence/absence still
  does not require host permissions. TODO(crbug.com/576028087) Consider
  requiring host permissions for matching custom headers.
- Mark a rule as requiring host permissions (`requires_host_permissions = true`
  in `flat::EmbedderConditions`, bumping `kIndexedRulesetFormatVersion`)
  if any condition in its `responseHeaders` or `excludedResponseHeaders`
  matches on the values of a non-allowlisted header.
- When an extension lacks host access to a request or navigation, skip
  rules that require host permissions entirely during matching (rather
  than partially evaluating their conditions or dropping their action
  after matching), allowing lower-priority rules that do not require
  host permissions to match instead.

This behavior is guarded by the enabled-by-default feature flag
`kDeclarativeNetRequestRestrictResponseHeaderValueMatching`.

Design doc (internal):
https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EciUIpGgLkpEqJ-MMUPTF1184IUitUy8MlwXYGskwfA/edit?usp=sharing&resourcekey=0-NXKn-lqRk_Y7GQGXEQWn1g

Fixed: 497744349, 549603220
Change-Id: I091cec3d3cec4aac8da7d0ee84e5559cd74234b4
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8547765
Commit-Queue: Kelvin Jiang <kelvinjiang@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Andrea Orru <andreaorru@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1724187}
(cherry picked from commit 22a2af917b63)

[FlyWeb] Hand port: in 156 DoEmbedderConditionsMatch() does not take the
request URL yet (that arrived with b878de30c0, hidden response headers), so
only `has_host_access` is added and the matchers are bound without the URL.
In RulesetMatcherBase::OnDidFinishNavigation() 156 has no error-document
branch (c06e1d94a2), so `has_host_access` is set on both RequestParams of
the 156 code. The two new tests that collided in ruleset_matcher_unittest.cc
(next to tests for b878de30c0 and c06e1d94a2) are left out.
